From: hashtagbasit
Subject: power: supply: qcom_battmgr: real power on SM8550-family firmware

On a Pocket FIT (SM8650) the firmware's battery power reading is stale: it
sat at 99.18 W while the battery took 19.7 W (2.3 A at 8.6 V).
UPower derives the charge and drain rate from power_now.

For the SM8550 variant, power_now is the battery's own current times its
voltage. (Steam's charging time comes from /run/vpower, written in user
space from fresh readings.)

---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -600,6 +600,17 @@
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_POWER_NOW:
 		val->intval = battmgr->status.power_now;
+		/*
+		 * The SM8550-family firmware's power reading goes stale: a Pocket
+		 * FIT reported a fixed 99.18 W while its battery took 19.7 W, and
+		 * UPower (and Steam through it) take the charge and drain rate
+		 * from here. Report the battery's own current times voltage.
+		 */
+		if (battmgr->variant == QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8550 && battmgr->status.voltage_now) {
+			s64 ua = abs(battmgr->status.current_now);
+
+			val->intval = (int)div_s64(ua * battmgr->status.voltage_now, 1000000);
+		}
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL_DESIGN:
 		if (unit != QCOM_BATTMGR_UNIT_mAh)
